          "distinct": true,
          "id": "12efdc9003dc914763a4a08e916065001e78cbee",
          "message": "Add a .lastlight agent-context rule for the DB-free test path\n\nCLAUDE.md documents the constrained-environment test path, but relies on\nan agent going and reading it. .lastlight/agent-context/*.md is prepended\nas AGENTS.md into every Last Light session for this repo, so the rule is\nin context from the first turn instead of being something to discover.\n\nSays the same thing as the CLAUDE.md section, tighter: npm test needs a\ndatabase and its failure means \"no database\", not a regression; run\ntest:sqlite, test:client, test:cli, lint and typecheck instead; and don't\nclaim to have verified an engine you couldn't run.\n\nThe layer is additive-only and testing.md collides with none of the\noperator-owned basenames (rules/security/soul), so it merges cleanly —\nverified with `lastlight repo config validate`.\n\nAlso drops the .lastlight/issue-* build artifacts committed back when\nbuild assets were written into the repo. They are externalized to the\nLast Light server now, so these are dead files that the repo-config fetch\ncounts as unrecognised on every run. Still in git history if wanted.",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-08T11:54:07+02:00",
          "tree_id": "cd59b95f7e162ba641b4694dd83a8eb567841677",
