          "message": "chore(deps): upgrade to TypeScript 7 (#1185)\n\n* chore(deps): upgrade to TypeScript 7\n\nSupersedes #1016. Type checking now runs on the native TypeScript 7\ncompiler, with the TypeScript 6.0 JS API installed side by side for the\ntools that still need it.\n\nPer the TS 7 release notes, the compiler is installed under the\n`@typescript/native` alias (providing `tsc`) while `typescript` is\naliased to `@typescript/typescript6` (providing the JS API and `tsc6`).\ntypescript-eslint hard-errors on TS >= 7.0 (typescript-eslint#10940) and\nvite-plugin-dts uses the JS API to emit declarations, so both keep\nrunning against the 6.0 API — no monkey-patching required.\n\nCode changes needed by TS 7:\n\n- `baseUrl` was removed in TS 7 (TS5102). Dropped from `tsconfig.json`,\n  `dev/tsconfig.json` and `dev/client/tsconfig.json`; all `paths` entries\n  were already tsconfig-relative, so resolution is unchanged.\n- Side-effect CSS imports now error (TS2882). Enabled\n  `allowArbitraryExtensions` and added `.d.css.ts` stubs next to the\n  three local stylesheets. `@xyflow/react/dist/style.css` ships no stub\n  of its own, so it is mapped through `paths` to a local one.\n- `tsconfig.client.json` now sets `types: [\"node\"]`, which\n  vite-plugin-dts needs to resolve `process` in `exportXlsx.ts` and\n  `thumbnail.ts` under the 6.0 API.\n\nVerified: lint, typecheck, build, check:exports, test:sqlite (2370),\ntest:client (5983) and test:cli all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: regenerate mcp-app html bundle\n\nThe checked-in `generated-html.ts` was produced by an older vite/rolldown\nthan the one in the lockfile, so `npm run build` left the tree dirty on a\nclean checkout. Regenerated with the current toolchain; the diff is the\nbundler's helper preamble and minifier output, not a source change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(client): ship type declarations for the published stylesheet\n\nTypeScript 7 rejects a side-effect import whose specifier has no type\ndeclarations (TS2882), so consumers on TS 7 following the documented\n`import 'drizzle-cube/client/styles.css'` failed to compile:\n\n    error TS2882: Cannot find module or type declarations for\n    side-effect import of 'drizzle-cube/client/styles.css'.\n\nThe client build now copies `styles.d.css.ts` into `dist/client/`, and\nthe `./client/styles.css` export gained a `types` condition pointing at\nit. Because the declaration is found through the exports map, consumers\ndo not need `allowArbitraryExtensions` in their own tsconfig.\n\nVerified against a packed tarball with tsc 7.0.2 under moduleResolution\nbundler, node16 and nodenext — all clean, and attw/publint unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
