          "distinct": false,
          "id": "e5b267d3638c6d1998b568cd8660107efe7b6eee",
          "message": "feat(client): redesign the gauge and give its thresholds a real editor\n\nThe gauge looked poor and its threshold bands could only be configured by\ntyping raw JSON into a text box.\n\nThe dial was drawn as a single thick progress arc with a hairline needle and an\nunformatted value. It also appeared to be a half-circle: the geometry placed the\ncentre at 0.7 of the height and sized the radius against the full height, so the\nbottom of what was meant to be a 270° sweep was clipped off the SVG.\n\nIt is now a 270° dial of thick rounded band segments - one per threshold, with\ngaps at the internal boundaries - plus numeric scale ticks at the boundaries, a\ntapered needle on a hub, and the measure label above the value below centre. The\ngeometry moved into `gaugeChartHelpers` as the testable seam, with\n`computeGaugeLayout` sizing the arc so its bounding box actually fits.\n`buildThresholdBands` now tiles the whole range, and the invariant that a band's\ncolour matches `resolveColor` at the same fraction is pinned by test. Values\nroute through `formatAxisValue`, so the dial reads 66.94 rather than 66.937, and\na percent format gives 66.9%. The hard-coded `#6366f1` fill and `#e2e8f0` track\nare gone in favour of theme variables.\n\nThe config panel gets a `thresholdBands` option type. The band editor shows one\nrow per band - a colour swatch and a number - with add and remove. A band's\nvalue is persisted as a 0-1 fraction of the min->max range, which is not what\nanyone wants to type, so the editor works in the gauge's own units and converts\non the way in and out: a 0-100 dial is edited as 50, not 0.5. Bands are kept\nsorted, so dragging one past another cannot corrupt the order, and a zero span\nfalls back to editing the fraction rather than dividing by zero.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-30T09:05:28+01:00",
          "tree_id": "f014d3eefc450d881a5b494915a915839036d997",
          "url": "https://github.com/cliftonc/drizzle-cube/commit/e5b267d3638c6d1998b568cd8660107efe7b6eee"
